1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,641
WebMCP makes a website callable by agents. WorkHub Goal Room makes each call state-aware, authority-checked, evidence-bound, and owner-controlled.

2
00:00:10,648 --> 00:00:22,415
A callable action is not automatically a legal action. An agent can act on stale state, bind evidence to the wrong Plan, or mistake a machine PASS for human acceptance.

3
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:47,672
Goal Room registers exactly five WebMCP tools. Every consequential call enters the same authority kernel, which revalidates actor, state, exact input, idempotency, evidence, and legal frontier. Invalid calls fail closed.

4
00:00:48,649 --> 00:01:04,317
Owner confirmation, verifier authorship, final acceptance, deployment, messaging, payments, and other external effects are intentionally not WebMCP tools.

5
00:01:05,320 --> 00:01:23,650
The agent proposed Plan v1, but work is blocked until the owner decides. The owner confirms the Plan. The agent claims an admitted step and submits exact candidate bytes and their SHA-256 digest.

6
00:01:24,660 --> 00:01:37,749
Candidate v1 enters deterministic verification and fails. The original evidence and FAIL receipt remain immutable. The agent submits corrected Candidate v2.

7
00:01:38,708 --> 00:01:48,662
The internal verifier records PASS. PASS does not accept the Goal. It only permits the agent to request completion for this exact candidate.

8
00:01:49,658 --> 00:02:04,124
The frontier moves to the owner. The agent and verifier are blocked. Only the owner can accept the verified candidate. After acceptance, no further governed action remains.

9
00:02:05,072 --> 00:02:20,841
The public repository contains the complete clean-room implementation, Apache-2.0 license, ninety tests, bounded reliability evidence, and run instructions. The demo uses synthetic browser-local state and creates no external effects.

10
00:02:21,822 --> 00:02:29,085
Humans and agents can share one state machine without sharing one authority level.
